raye-base (1.0~beta2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Chromebooks: map the top row of keys through keyd and show where to fix
    the sound.
  * FL Studio no longer downloads extra fonts on first start.
  * Game Mode turns on by itself while a Steam, Store or Windows game
    runs: full processor speed (it was refused before), the game
    scheduler, blur and transparency paused, and Best performance power
    mode while plugged in. Everything comes back when the game ends or
    crashes.
  * Ubuntu's upgrade guard starts with each upgrade run and fwupd leaves
    when idle, about 25 MB less memory at idle.
  * The kernel keeps a free-memory reserve sized to the RAM instead of a
    fixed 66 MB, and the disk, battery and network notices run once a
    minute instead of staying in memory.
  * X11 settings are written when X11 starts, not at every sign-in.
  * Starting Windows or the firmware settings from the boot menu no longer
    takes the boot screen away from Raye.

