raye-base (1.0~beta1) resolute; urgency=high

  * Raye starts without waiting on the boot menu: it shows only after a start
    that did not reach the desktop, and for 3 seconds (not 10) when Windows
    is on the disk.
  * The NVIDIA helper no longer runs before the sign-in screen on PCs without
    NVIDIA's driver; the start-up files carry only this PC's microcode.
  * The X11 helpers start with the first X11 program instead of at every
    sign-in. Ctrl+Win+Enter turns the screen reader on or off.
  * The NVIDIA Control Panel is installed with the driver; the Clock and
    Graphics Card apps come with the desktop.
  * Windows programs start in their own folder, 32-bit ones get 4 GB, and
    Store packages (.msix, .appx) open with Raye.
  * No switch to the Raye kernel while NVIDIA's prebuilt modules are
    installed (they only load on the standard kernel).
  * Old BIOS PCs: GRUB for BIOS comes with the system.
  * Boot menu: Try Raye Linux without installing, in English and French.
  * VirtualBox and VMware guest tools come with the desktop (they only
    start inside their own kind of virtual machine), like QEMU's already did.
  * On AMD cards with a kernel that lacks the RGBA8888 fix, the sign-in
    screen and the desktop draw the pointer themselves, so the screen no
    longer stays black; AMD PCs the graphics fallback had left in safe
    graphics try normal graphics once more after this update.

