raye-base (0.3~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The system now calls itself Raye Linux 0.3 Beta.
  * New in the system: Raye Calendar, Control Panel and Registry Editor.
    Task Manager replaces System Monitor.
  * Ubuntu packages come from a mirror list (archive, then ca. and
    gb.archive.ubuntu.com). Older machines are moved over on upgrade,
    with a copy of their old ubuntu.sources.
  * The night background shows from the moment GRUB starts, so no black
    screen while the system loads. No boot menu after an update restart,
    and no text at shutdown.
  * PackageKit no longer installs or restarts during Raye's updates at
    restart. The quiet boot command line now reaches existing installs,
    and the disk unlock scripts get the realpath they call.
  * The sign-in screen comes back when a session is ended from outside
    (loginctl terminate-user, out of memory) instead of leaving a black
    screen.
  * Daily restore points with space limits: fewer of them, at most a
    tenth of the disk. Btrfs Assistant is installed as Restore Points.
  * Windows programs use the new Raye Night and Raye Day greys.

