raye-base (0.1~dev6) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Adding a software source works again. aptsources needs a template
    named after the system, and there was none: add-apt-repository,
    software-properties and Synaptic's repository dialog all stopped on
    NoDistroTemplateException before doing any work. raye-release now
    ships it, so an upgrade of python-apt cannot take it away.
  * Raye in a virtual machine works over SPICE with nothing to set: the
    clipboard, the resize to the window and a visible cursor. The agent
    was only recommended, and the image build never installs a
    recommended package, so it was absent from every image so far.
  * Firefox no longer offers to install a browser add-on named after
    another desktop.
  * The boot menu of a machine with two or three systems on it reads in
    plain names: "Windows" and "Fedora Linux 42" rather than "Windows
    Boot Manager (on /dev/nvme0n1p1)". Two systems of the same name keep
    what tells them apart. Only the titles change -- what boots, the
    entry ids and the icon classes come out byte for byte the same, the
    new menu is checked before it is put in place, and a pass that fails
    never fails a kernel update.
  * The mouse pointer shows up in a virtual machine. The desktop was
    leaving it to the graphics card's cursor plane, which a console or a
    SPICE viewer does not show: the pointer worked and was invisible.
  * Everyday tools come with the system: the two software managers, a
    drop-down terminal, Google Drive and network shares in the file
    manager, disk snapshots, the ALSA/JACK/PulseAudio and camera faces of
    the audio server, and the usual terminal tools.
  * The repository dialog calls the system by its full name. It was the
    one place out of six that showed the version without the word the
    other five carry, so Synaptic listed "Raye Linux 0.1" while the login
    screen, the terminal banner and the installer all said "Raye Linux
    0.1 Beta".

 -- techoraye <190692880+techoraye@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 11:44:17 +0000

raye-base (0.1~dev5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * zstd for a smaller, faster initramfs.
  * The KDE wallet opens at login (pam_kwallet5), phones show up over
    USB (mtp-probe), fingerprint readers work (fprintd).
  * Windows programs: a ready space is prepared in the background after
    login (core fonts, DXVK, vkd3d-proton), so a .exe opens in about
    three seconds with nothing to answer. Free fonts and Xvfb shipped;
    installers a profile needs run on an invisible screen. winetricks
    may no longer accept a file whose SHA-256 does not match.
  * The launcher stopped upgrading every space on each launch: Wine
    writes its timestamp with a Windows line ending.
  * Wine 11 from WineHQ (key checked by fingerprint, pinned; the
    archive's Wine 10 kept out), with ntsync loaded at boot and opened
    for the person at the computer. gamescope and vulkan-tools for games.
  * "Restart to Windows" on computers that have it: one click starts
    Windows next time only (BootNext), without the boot menu. Allowed
    for the person at the computer, like a restart; the menu entry shows
    only when a Windows entry is found at boot.
  * raye-kernel: the Raye key and the steps to switch kernels safely. The
    key is queued for MokManager with a six-digit code, and the kernel is
    installed at the next boot only once the key is enrolled, so Secure
    Boot never meets a kernel it does not know. Ubuntu's kernel stays.
  * raye-kernel: the kernel image is signed with a boot key that
    MokManager accepts, and modules with a separate key; the kernel gets
    one trial boot and Ubuntu's stays the default until it has started.
  * raye-kernel: a disk the TPM opens gets a second TPM binding for the
    Raye kernel after its first start, so it keeps opening by itself;
    "raye-kernel-setup rebind" does the same with the disk password.
  * raye-kernel-setup status says "enrolled" only when the kernel is
    queued for the next boot, not for a key left in the firmware.

